{
  "case": "compound",
  "proves": "A compound statement whose bodies only make calls of a rule family, and whose header has no effect, is suppressed with that family, every site inside it included. A statement with a body that also returns, or a range over a channel, keeps its mutants. An if or a switch whose header calls an API outside the families keeps its deletion, and its condition or its case expressions are suppressed, because they only choose which body runs.",
  "fixture": "warn logs an error that is not nil. fail logs it and reports it. each logs every value of a list, and drain every value of a channel. flush logs the error that a write returns. level calls a function in a switch's header and logs whether it fails. sign logs the sign of a number in a switch. The tests check the result of fail, the channel after drain, the bytes that flush writes and the calls that level makes.",
